28:["$","$L54",null,{"type":"multiple","children":[["$","$L55",null,{"title":"Actions stay queued forever","id":"actions-stay-queued-forever","children":["$","p",null,{"children":["At least one worker's ",["$","code",null,{"children":"platform_properties"}]," must satisfy what your actions\nrequest, and every requested key must be declared in the scheduler's\n",["$","code",null,{"children":"supported_platform_properties"}],". Starting with just ",["$","code",null,{"children":"cpu_count: \"minimum\""}],"\non the scheduler and ",["$","code",null,{"children":"cpu_count: { values: [\"1\"] }"}]," on the worker unblocks\nmost local setups.\n",["$","$L6",null,{"href":"/remote-execution/platform-properties","children":"Platform properties"}]," has the full\nmatching rules and the scheduler's own diagnostic logging."]}]}],["$","$L55",null,{"title":"'instance_name' not configured for ''","id":"instance-name-not-configured","children":["$","p",null,{"children":["Every service in the example config omits ",["$","code",null,{"children":"instance_name"}],", so it defaults to\nthe empty string, the same default Bazel uses when you don't pass\n",["$","code",null,{"children":"--remote_instance_name"}],". If you add an ",["$","code",null,{"children":"instance_name"}]," server-side, pass\nthe matching flag client-side, or every request fails this way."]}]}],["$","$L55",null,{"title":"The worker exits immediately on macOS","id":"the-worker-exits-immediately-on-macos","children":["$","p",null,{"children":[["$","code",null,{"children":"use_namespaces"}]," and ",["$","code",null,{"children":"use_mount_namespace"}]," are Linux-only and default to\n",["$","code",null,{"children":"false"}],". Setting either to ",["$","code",null,{"children":"true"}]," on an unsupported platform makes the\nworker exit at startup. Leave them unset for local testing."]}]}],["$","$L55",null,{"title":"Stale state between runs","id":"stale-state-between-runs","children":["$","p",null,{"children":["Everything the example config writes lives under\n",["$","code",null,{"children":"/tmp/forge-local-rbe-test/"}],". Stop the server and delete that tree for\na genuinely cold start; ",["$","code",null,{"children":"bazel clean"}]," only clears Bazel's side."]}]}],["$","$L55",null,{"title":"Port already in use","id":"port-already-in-use","children":["$","p",null,{"children":["Usually a previous run still holding ",["$","code",null,{"children":"50051"}]," or ",["$","code",null,{"children":"50061"}],", or the compose\nstack still up. ",["$","code",null,{"children":"docker compose rm --stop -f"}]," in\n",["$","code",null,{"children":"deployment-examples/docker-compose"}]," clears the second case."]}]}]]}]
